commit.message:
fix(replicate): cancel abandoned image predictions on abort and poll timeout (#24571)

## Background

Replicate predictions keep running — and keep consuming compute — until
they reach a terminal status. `ReplicateImageModel` abandons polling in
two situations without telling Replicate, so the abandoned prediction
keeps going:

- the caller aborts through `abortSignal` while the model polls for a
result, or
- polling gives up because `maxPollAttempts` was exhausted.

In both cases the prediction's cancel endpoint (`POST
/predictions/{prediction_id}/cancel`, per the provider's OpenAPI spec)
was never used. The gap was found by auditing the provider against its
spec.

The prediction response also carries a `urls.cancel` value, but that is
response-body data and therefore not a safe request target for a
credentialed request. This PR no longer uses it.

## Summary

- **`src/cancel-prediction.ts`** — best-effort cancel helper:
- URL is built from configuration as
`${baseURL}/predictions/${encodePathSegment(predictionId)}/cancel`;
nothing from the response body is used as a request target.
- Sent with the repo's normal API helper (`postToApi`) and fresh
provider headers (`combineHeaders(await resolve(config.headers))`): no
per-call headers and no create-request idempotency key.
- No abort signal, no retries; errors (network failures, non-2xx
responses, header resolution failures) are swallowed. Call sites are
fire-and-forget, so a cancel can never mask, replace, or delay the
original abort/timeout error and never produces an unhandled rejection.
- **`ReplicateImageModel`** — cancels the current prediction when the
caller aborts while polling and when polling gives up after
`maxPollAttempts`. The original `AbortError` / timeout `Error` is
rethrown unchanged. The response schema now requires `id` and no longer
accepts `urls.cancel`.
- **Video model** — reverted to `origin/main`. Cancelling video
predictions from `doStart`/`doStatus` changes the V4 video lifecycle
semantics (start is fire-and-forget, status signals are single checks,
and start/status can run in different processes in workflow/serialized
flows). It needs a spec-level hook instead; see Future Work.
- **Docs** — the Replicate provider docs describe image-only
cancellation, which applies while polling after the prediction has been
created, not during the initial create request (`Prefer: wait`).
- **Tests** — new `cancel-prediction.test.ts` (posts to the
config-derived URL with the auth header, no idempotency key, no signal;
swallows network and 500 errors and header-resolution errors) and
updated image-model tests (the rethrown error is asserted by type, name,
and message; the cancel request is sent exactly once; no cancel after
successful completion).
- Patch changeset for `@ai-sdk/replicate`.

## End-to-End Verification

### Prerequisite and limit

The live reproduction needs `REPLICATE_API_TOKEN`. It is **blocked in
this environment**: the token in `examples/ai-functions/.env` has length
0 (`node --env-file=... -e
"console.log((process.env.REPLICATE_API_TOKEN||'').length)"` prints
`0`), the variable is not set in the shell, and no Replicate CLI token
exists. The live script
(`/tmp/repro-replicate-cancel-prediction/repro.mjs`) therefore exits
with `Error: REPLICATE_API_TOKEN is not set`, so live verification
against the Replicate API did not happen.

Instead, the public `generateImage` API is exercised against a local
HTTP stand-in for the Replicate API, configured through the provider's
public `baseURL` option. This runs the real provider and SDK code
(create request, SDK-owned polling, abort, cancel request) but not the
Replicate service itself.

### Setup / build

```bash
cd /private/tmp/ai-fix-replicate-cancel-prediction
command pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
command pnpm exec turbo build --filter=ai... --filter=@ai-sdk/replicate...
```

Both runs were executed from `examples/ai-functions`, whose
`node_modules` are pnpm workspace links, so `ai` and `@ai-sdk/replicate`
resolve to this checkout's locally built `packages/ai` and
`packages/replicate`, not to published registry versions.

### Run

```bash
cd /private/tmp/ai-fix-replicate-cancel-prediction/examples/ai-functions
node --input-type=module < /tmp/repro-replicate-cancel-prediction/repro-local-image.mjs
```

### Reproduction script
(`/tmp/repro-replicate-cancel-prediction/repro-local-image.mjs`)

Kept outside the checkout. The stub never completes a prediction, so the
call is abandoned twice — once by the caller aborting, once by
exhausting `maxPollAttempts` — and a third time with a prediction that
succeeds. The prediction it returns points `urls.cancel` at a second,
"attacker" server so the script can show that response data is never
used as a request target.

```js
// Local stand-in for the Replicate API, used because the live token is not
// available in this environment. It exercises the public `ai` API against this
// checkout's provider: a prediction is created, never completes, and the call is
// abandoned (caller abort, poll-attempt exhaustion). The script prints whether
// the provider sent a cancel request for the prediction, and whether it ever
// followed the untrusted `urls.cancel` URL from the response body.
import { createServer } from 'node:http';
import { generateImage } from 'ai';
import { createReplicate } from '@ai-sdk/replicate';

const cancelRequests = [];
const attackerRequests = [];
let apiServer;
let attackerServer;

const predictionFor = origin => ({
  id: 'pred-123',
  status: 'processing',
  output: null,
  error: null,
  urls: {
    get: `${origin}/v1/predictions/pred-123`,
    // untrusted response data: must never be used as a request target
    cancel: `http://127.0.0.1:${attackerServer.address().port}/steal`,
  },
});

attackerServer = createServer(async (request, response) => {
  attackerRequests.push(request.url);
  response.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' });
  response.end('{}');
});
await new Promise(resolve => attackerServer.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', resolve));

apiServer = createServer(async (request, response) => {
  const origin = `http://127.0.0.1:${apiServer.address().port}`;
  for await (const _chunk of request) {
    // drain
  }

  if (
    request.method === 'POST' &&
    request.url === '/v1/predictions/pred-123/cancel'
  ) {
    cancelRequests.push({
      url: request.url,
      authorization: request.headers.authorization,
      idempotencyKey: request.headers['idempotency-key'],
      userAgent: request.headers['user-agent'],
    });
    response.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' });
    response.end(
      JSON.stringify({ ...predictionFor(origin), status: 'canceled' }),
    );
    return;
  }

  if (request.method === 'POST') {
    response.writeHead(201, { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' });
    response.end(JSON.stringify(predictionFor(origin)));
    return;
  }

  if (request.method === 'GET' && request.url === '/v1/predictions/pred-123') {
    response.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' });
    response.end(JSON.stringify(predictionFor(origin)));
    return;
  }

  response.writeHead(404);
  response.end('not found');
});
await new Promise(resolve => apiServer.listen(0, '127.0.0.1', resolve));

const baseURL = `http://127.0.0.1:${apiServer.address().port}/v1`;
const replicate = createReplicate({ apiToken: 'test-token', baseURL });
const model = replicate.image('black-forest-labs/flux-1.1-pro');

console.log(`stub Replicate API at ${baseURL}`);

// image model: caller aborts while the provider polls
cancelRequests.length = 0;
attackerRequests.length = 0;
try {
  await generateImage({
    model,
    prompt: 'a red bicycle next to a lighthouse',
    providerOptions: {
      replicate: {
        maxWaitTimeInSeconds: 1,
        pollIntervalMillis: 150,
        maxPollAttempts: 100,
      },
    },
    maxRetries: 0,
    abortSignal: AbortSignal.timeout(1200),
  });
  console.log('image abort: generateImage resolved');
} catch (error) {
  console.log(`image abort: generateImage threw ${error?.name}: ${error?.message}`);
}
await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 300));
console.log(`image abort: cancel requests received: ${cancelRequests.length}`);
console.log(
  `image abort: cancel request: ${JSON.stringify(cancelRequests[0] ?? null)}`,
);
console.log(`image abort: untrusted cancel URL requests: ${attackerRequests.length}`);

// image model: polling gives up after maxPollAttempts
cancelRequests.length = 0;
attackerRequests.length = 0;
try {
  await generateImage({
    model,
    prompt: 'a red bicycle next to a lighthouse',
    providerOptions: {
      replicate: {
        maxWaitTimeInSeconds: 1,
        pollIntervalMillis: 50,
        maxPollAttempts: 3,
      },
    },
    maxRetries: 0,
  });
  console.log('image timeout: generateImage resolved');
} catch (error) {
  console.log(
    `image timeout: generateImage threw ${error?.name}: ${error?.message}`,
  );
}
await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 300));
console.log(
  `image timeout: cancel requests received: ${cancelRequests.length}`,
);
console.log(
  `image timeout: untrusted cancel URL requests: ${attackerRequests.length}`,
);

// image model: successful completion must not cancel
cancelRequests.length = 0;
apiServer.removeAllListeners('request');
apiServer.on('request', async (request, response) => {
  const origin = `http://127.0.0.1:${apiServer.address().port}`;
  for await (const _chunk of request) {
    // drain
  }

  if (request.method === 'POST' && request.url === '/v1/predictions/pred-123/cancel') {
    cancelRequests.push(request.url);
  }

  response.writeHead(200, { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' });
  response.end(
    JSON.stringify({
      ...predictionFor(origin),
      status: 'succeeded',
      output: [`http://127.0.0.1:${apiServer.address().port}/out.webp`],
    }),
  );
});
try {
  await generateImage({ model, prompt: 'a red bicycle', maxRetries: 0 });
  console.log('image success: generateImage resolved');
} catch (error) {
  console.log(`image success: generateImage threw ${error?.name}: ${error?.message}`);
}
await new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(resolve, 300));
console.log(`image success: cancel requests received: ${cancelRequests.length}`);

apiServer.close();
attackerServer.close();
```

### Observed before the fix

Same script, same locally built packages, `packages/replicate/src`
restored from `origin/main`:

```
stub Replicate API at http://127.0.0.1:49937/v1
image abort: generateImage threw AbortError: Delay was aborted
image abort: cancel requests received: 0
image abort: cancel request: null
image abort: untrusted cancel URL requests: 0
image timeout: generateImage threw Error: Replicate image generation did not complete after 3 polling attempts.
image timeout: cancel requests received: 0
image timeout: untrusted cancel URL requests: 0
image success: generateImage resolved
image success: cancel requests received: 0
```

### Observed after the fix

```
stub Replicate API at http://127.0.0.1:49951/v1
image abort: generateImage threw AbortError: Delay was aborted
image abort: cancel requests received: 1
image abort: cancel request: {"url":"/v1/predictions/pred-123/cancel","authorization":"Bearer test-token","userAgent":"ai-sdk-replicate/3.0.76 ai-sdk-provider-utils/5.0.75 node.js/24"}
image abort: untrusted cancel URL requests: 0
image timeout: generateImage threw Error: Replicate image generation did not complete after 3 polling attempts.
image timeout: cancel requests received: 1
image timeout: untrusted cancel URL requests: 0
image success: generateImage resolved
image success: cancel requests received: 0
```

The abort error and the timeout error are unchanged in both runs. After
the fix, the cancel request goes to the config-derived path with the
configured `Authorization` header, no `idempotency-key`, and the
untrusted `urls.cancel` host is never contacted. A successful prediction
sends no cancel request.

### Provider flow exercised and limits

- Exercised: `generateImage` → `ReplicateImageModel.doGenerate` →
SDK-side polling → caller abort or poll-attempt exhaustion → `POST
{baseURL}/predictions/{id}/cancel`.
- Not exercised: the live Replicate API (no token, see above), and video
generation, which this PR reverts to `origin/main`.
- Cancellation is not attempted while the initial create request is in
flight, because no prediction ID exists yet.

## Checklist

- [x] All commits are signed (PRs with unsigned commits cannot be
merged)
- [x] Tests have been added / updated (for bug fixes / features)
- [x] Documentation has been added / updated (for bug fixes / features)
- [x] A _patch_ changeset for relevant packages has been added (for bug
fixes / features - run `pnpm changeset` in the project root)
- [x] I have reviewed this pull request (self-review)

## Future Work

- Cancel video predictions too. That needs a `doCancel` hook in the
`VideoModelV4` spec, called from the core start/status flow when it
gives up on a poll timeout or observes an abort — the model cannot
observe these today, and `doStart`/`doStatus` may run in different
processes in workflow/serialized flows. Adding the hook is a spec change
and needs an ADR.
- The separate PR that adds the `aborted` prediction status is
intentionally not touched here.

## Related Issues

No linked issue. The gap was found by auditing the provider against its
OpenAPI spec cached in
[gr2m/ai-provider-monitor](https://github.com/gr2m/ai-provider-monitor).

