fix(black-forest-labs): handle webhook submit responses without polling URL (#24565)

## Background

`@ai-sdk/black-forest-labs` documents the `webhookUrl` provider option
and forwards it as `webhook_url` on image submit requests. Black Forest
Labs answers submit requests with either `AsyncResponse` (includes
`polling_url`) or `AsyncWebhookResponse` (includes `webhook_url` and
`status`, but no `polling_url`).

When a webhook was set, the live API returned the webhook-shaped
response:

```
submit response keys: [ 'cost', 'id', 'input_mp', 'output_mp', 'status', 'webhook_url' ]
submit response: {"id":"447d8898-c9e6-46a2-8725-4787c9a9f9e9","status":"processing","webhook_url":"https://example.com/ai-sdk-bfl-webhook","cost":1.4000000000000001}
```

The submit response schema required `polling_url`, so `generateImage`
failed with `Invalid JSON response`. A follow-up probe of the documented
`GET /v1/get_result?id=` endpoint for the same request id showed the job
becomes visible after a short propagation delay, then reports `Ready`
with `result.sample`:

```
attempt 1: HTTP 404 status="Task not found"
attempt 2: HTTP 404 status="Task not found"
attempt 3: HTTP 200 status="Ready" hasResult=true sample=https://delivery.us2.bfl.ai/...
```

## Summary

- Make `polling_url` optional in the image submit response schema and
accept webhook-shaped responses.
- When no `polling_url` is returned, poll the documented `get_result`
endpoint at the configured base URL by request id. This is a best-effort
fallback: the call still waits for completion, bounded by
`pollTimeoutMillis`, and the webhook is delivered as well.
- Treat transient HTTP 404 / `Task not found` responses as pending while
the job is being registered.
- Cap the not-found retry grace period separately from the overall poll
timeout (`MAX_TASK_NOT_FOUND_ATTEMPTS = 20`, about 10s at the default
500ms interval). A task that never becomes visible now fails with `Black
Forest Labs task <id> was not found via get_result before timing out`
instead of the generic `Black Forest Labs generation timed out.`
- Add regression tests for the webhook-shaped submit response, the
transient 404 retry, a 200 `Task not found` response, a persistent 404
`Task not found`, a 404 with a non-not-found body (no retry), and an
abort during the not-found retry delay.
- Document that the `get_result` fallback is best effort and subject to
`pollTimeoutMillis`.

## End-to-End Verification

Exercised the real `generateImage` flow plus `@ai-sdk/black-forest-labs`
image model against the live Black Forest Labs API (`flux-2-klein-4b`,
one generation per run). Both runs imported this checkout's locally
built packages: the script lives outside the checkout, `node` runs from
`examples/ai-functions`, and the workspace symlinks there resolve `ai`
and `@ai-sdk/black-forest-labs` to this checkout's `packages/*/dist`
rather than registry versions.

Prerequisites: `BFL_API_KEY` in the environment. The script also
performs one direct submit request to print the raw response shape.

Setup and run (from the repository root):

```bash
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm exec turbo build --filter=ai... --filter=@ai-sdk/black-forest-labs... --output-logs=errors-only

cd examples/ai-functions
node --env-file=<path to a .env containing BFL_API_KEY> --input-type=module < /tmp/repro-bfl-webhook-response/repro.mjs
```

Reproduction script `/tmp/repro-bfl-webhook-response/repro.mjs`:

```js
import { generateImage } from 'ai';
import { blackForestLabs } from '@ai-sdk/black-forest-labs';

const apiKey = process.env.BFL_API_KEY;
if (!apiKey) {
  throw new Error('BFL_API_KEY is missing');
}

const modelId = 'flux-2-klein-4b';
const webhookUrl = 'https://example.com/ai-sdk-bfl-webhook';

console.log('=== direct submit with webhook ===');
const submitResponse = await fetch(`https://api.bfl.ai/v1/${modelId}`, {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    'content-type': 'application/json',
    'x-key': apiKey,
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({ prompt: 'a red apple', webhook_url: webhookUrl }),
});
console.log('submit HTTP status:', submitResponse.status);
const submitJson = await submitResponse.json();
console.log('submit response keys:', Object.keys(submitJson).sort());
console.log(
  'submit response:',
  JSON.stringify({
    id: submitJson.id,
    status: submitJson.status,
    webhook_url: submitJson.webhook_url,
    polling_url: submitJson.polling_url,
    cost: submitJson.cost,
  }),
);

if (typeof submitJson.id === 'string') {
  const resultResponse = await fetch(
    `https://api.bfl.ai/v1/get_result?id=${encodeURIComponent(submitJson.id)}`,
    { headers: { 'x-key': apiKey } },
  );
  console.log('get_result HTTP status:', resultResponse.status);
  const resultJson = await resultResponse.json();
  console.log(
    'get_result snapshot:',
    JSON.stringify({
      id: resultJson.id,
      status: resultJson.status,
      hasResult: resultJson.result != null,
      keys: Object.keys(resultJson).sort(),
    }),
  );
}

console.log('\n=== generateImage with webhookUrl ===');
try {
  const { image, providerMetadata } = await generateImage({
    model: blackForestLabs.image(modelId),
    prompt: 'a red apple',
    providerOptions: {
      blackForestLabs: { webhookUrl },
    },
  });
  console.log('generateImage succeeded');
  console.log('image bytes:', image.uint8Array.length);
  console.log(
    'providerMetadata:',
    JSON.stringify(providerMetadata?.blackForestLabs),
  );
} catch (error) {
  console.log('generateImage failed');
  console.log('error name:', error?.name);
  console.log('error message:', error?.message);
  if (error?.cause != null) {
    console.log('error cause:', String(error.cause).slice(0, 600));
  }
}
```

Before (origin/main):

```
=== direct submit with webhook ===
submit HTTP status: 200
submit response keys: [ 'cost', 'id', 'input_mp', 'output_mp', 'status', 'webhook_url' ]
submit response: {"id":"447d8898-c9e6-46a2-8725-4787c9a9f9e9","status":"processing","webhook_url":"https://example.com/ai-sdk-bfl-webhook","cost":1.4000000000000001}
get_result HTTP status: 404
get_result snapshot: {"id":"447d8898-c9e6-46a2-8725-4787c9a9f9e9","status":"Task not found","hasResult":false,"keys":["details","id","preview","progress","result","status"]}

=== generateImage with webhookUrl ===
generateImage failed
error name: AI_APICallError
error message: Invalid JSON response
error cause: AI_TypeValidationError: Type validation failed: Value: {"id":"df7da09f-cf7a-4bbe-a0c5-fd8034a59105","status":"processing","webhook_url":"https://example.com/ai-sdk-bfl-webhook","cost":1.4000000000000001,"input_mp":0,"output_mp":1}.
Error message: [
  {
    "expected": "string",
    "code": "invalid_type",
    "path": [
      "polling_url"
    ],
    "message": "Invalid input: expected string, received undefined"
  }
]
```

After (this branch):

```
=== direct submit with webhook ===
submit HTTP status: 200
submit response keys: [ 'cost', 'id', 'input_mp', 'output_mp', 'status', 'webhook_url' ]
submit response: {"id":"dea44264-ff42-43ca-af27-bd2efa86dd4a","status":"processing","webhook_url":"https://example.com/ai-sdk-bfl-webhook","cost":1.4000000000000001}
get_result HTTP status: 404
get_result snapshot: {"id":"dea44264-ff42-43ca-af27-bd2efa86dd4a","status":"Task not found","hasResult":false,"keys":["details","id","preview","progress","result","status"]}

=== generateImage with webhookUrl ===
generateImage succeeded
image bytes: 265228
providerMetadata: {"images":[{"seed":3063243409,"start_time":1793848302.4669924,"cost":1.4000000000000001,"inputMegapixels":0,"outputMegapixels":1}]}
```

The direct `get_result` probe in this run still answered HTTP 404 `Task
not found` while `generateImage` completed, which is the propagation
delay described above. Whether the SDK's own fallback retried through a
404 in that run is not observable from the script; that path is covered
by unit tests instead:

```
retries get_result while a webhook job is not yet registered
retries get_result when the poll response status is Task not found
fails with a clear error when get_result keeps answering 404 Task not found
gives up on Task not found without waiting for the overall poll timeout
does not retry get_result 404 responses that are not Task not found
rejects with AbortError when aborted during the not-found retry delay
```

The transient 404s were also observed directly with
`/tmp/repro-bfl-webhook-response/poll-get-result.mjs`, which polls
`get_result` for a submitted id:

```js
const apiKey = process.env.BFL_API_KEY;
const ids = [
  '447d8898-c9e6-46a2-8725-4787c9a9f9e9',
  'df7da09f-cf7a-4bbe-a0c5-fd8034a59105',
];

for (const id of ids) {
  console.log(`\n=== polling get_result for ${id} ===`);
  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= 15; attempt++) {
    const response = await fetch(
      `https://api.bfl.ai/v1/get_result?id=${encodeURIComponent(id)}`,
      { headers: { 'x-key': apiKey } },
    );
    const body = await response.json().catch(() => null);
    console.log(
      `attempt ${attempt}: HTTP ${response.status} status=${JSON.stringify(body?.status)} hasResult=${body?.result != null} sample=${body?.result?.sample ?? '-'} error=${body?.error ?? body?.details ? JSON.stringify(body?.details) : '-'}`,
    );
    if (body?.status === 'Ready' || body?.status === 'Error') break;
    await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 2000));
  }
}
```

Output:

```
=== polling get_result for 447d8898-c9e6-46a2-8725-4787c9a9f9e9 ===
attempt 1: HTTP 404 status="Task not found" hasResult=false sample=- error=-
attempt 2: HTTP 404 status="Task not found" hasResult=false sample=- error=-
attempt 3: HTTP 200 status="Ready" hasResult=true sample=https://delivery.us2.bfl.ai/...
```

Unit tests, type checking, and formatting:

```bash
cd packages/black-forest-labs
command pnpm test         # 208 tests passed (node + edge)
command pnpm type-check   # tsc --build passed

cd ../..
command pnpm fix                          # no changes needed
command pnpm run-verifiers --modified     # no applicable verifiers
command pnpm discover-guidelines --modified  # no applicable guidelines
```

Limitation: only one webhook generation per run because each costs
credits. The webhook receiver at `example.com` was not exercised;
`generateImage` waits for the image via `get_result` polling, not via
the callback.

## Checklist

- [x] All commits are signed (PRs with unsigned commits cannot be
merged)
- [x] Tests have been added / updated (for bug fixes / features)
- [x] Documentation has been added / updated (for bug fixes / features)
- [x] A _patch_ changeset for relevant packages has been added (for bug
fixes / features - run `pnpm changeset` in the project root)
- [x] I have reviewed this pull request (self-review)

## Related Issues

The gap was found by auditing the provider against its OpenAPI spec
cached in https://github.com/gr2m/ai-provider-monitor.

