commit.message:
fix(cohere): emit source stream parts for citations (#24570)

Stacked on #24574; GitHub will retarget to `main` once #24574 merges.

## Background

Cohere's chat API emits `citation-start` / `citation-end` stream events
when documents are passed for RAG. The non-streaming path maps
`message.citations` to `source` parts, so `generateText` returns
`sources`. The streaming path ignored the `citation-start` events, so
`streamText` returned no `sources` even though the model cited the
documents.

The gap was found by auditing `@ai-sdk/cohere` against its OpenAPI spec,
cached in
[gr2m/ai-provider-monitor](https://github.com/gr2m/ai-provider-monitor).

## Summary

- Use the shared `cohereCitationSchema` and `mapCohereCitationToSource`
from `cohere-citations.ts` (added in #24574) in both `doGenerate` and
`doStream`.
- Map every citation in a `citation-start` stream event to a `source`
stream part, using the same mapping as the non-streaming path (same
`mediaType`, `title` fallback, and `providerMetadata.cohere` shape).
- Accept the streaming citation payload as documented by the API:
`delta`, `delta.message`, and `delta.message.citations` are all
optional, and citations can be a single citation or an array.
- Ignore `citation-start` events without citations, and skip citations
that only reference tool output, matching `generateText`.
- `citation-end` remains a no-op; source parts are complete when
emitted.
- Add regression tests and a fixture captured from the live API, and
document Cohere sources in the provider docs.

## End-to-End Verification

Prerequisite: `COHERE_API_KEY` in the environment (loaded with `node
--env-file` from the local `examples/ai-functions/.env`, value not
printed). Reproduction-only file lives outside the checkout at
`/tmp/repro-cohere-stream-citations/repro.mjs`.

`/tmp/repro-cohere-stream-citations/repro.mjs`:

```js
import { generateText, streamText } from 'ai';
import { cohere } from '@ai-sdk/cohere';

const model = cohere('command-a-03-2025');

const prompt = [
  {
    type: 'text',
    text: 'What is the capital of the fictional country Zephyria? Answer in one short sentence.',
  },
  {
    type: 'file',
    data: Buffer.from(
      'Zephyria is a fictional country. Its capital city is Marrowdale, a coastal city known for its lighthouses.',
    ).toString('base64'),
    mediaType: 'text/plain',
    filename: 'zephyria.txt',
  },
];

const generate = await generateText({
  model,
  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: prompt }],
});
console.log('=== generateText ===');
console.log('text:', generate.text);
console.log('sources:', JSON.stringify(generate.sources, null, 2));

const stream = streamText({
  model,
  messages: [{ role: 'user', content: prompt }],
  includeRawChunks: true,
});

console.log('=== streamText ===');
let streamedText = '';
for await (const part of stream.fullStream) {
  if (part.type === 'source') {
    console.log('source part:', JSON.stringify(part, null, 2));
  }
  if (
    part.type === 'raw' &&
    String(part.rawValue?.type ?? '').startsWith('citation')
  ) {
    console.log('raw citation chunk:', JSON.stringify(part.rawValue));
  }
  if (part.type === 'text-delta') {
    streamedText += part.text;
  }
}
console.log('text:', streamedText);
console.log('sources:', JSON.stringify(await stream.sources, null, 2));
```

