commit.message:
fix(openai): surface Chat Completions refusals as text content (#24567)

## Background

The Chat Completions model (`openai.chat(...)`) never read
`message.refusal` (non-streaming) or `delta.refusal` (streaming) from
the OpenAI API. When the model refuses a request, OpenAI returns
`content: null` and puts the answer in `refusal`, so the AI SDK produced
empty text with a `stop` finish reason — the refusal message was
silently dropped and the response looked like a normal completion.

This is most visible with structured outputs (`response_format`
