commit.message:
fix(openai): handle refusal content parts in the Responses API (#24572)

## Background

The OpenAI Responses API returns an assistant `message` output item, and
its `content` array is `OutputTextContent | RefusalContent` in the
OpenAPI spec (`OutputMessageContent`). The provider only modeled `{
type: 'output_text', ... }` content parts.

When the model declines a request, the API returns a `refusal` content
part instead. Because the response schema rejected that part, every
non-streaming Responses call that hit a refusal failed with
`APICallError: Invalid JSON response` instead of surfacing the refusal,
and streaming dropped the `response.refusal.delta` /
`response.refusal.done` events silently, so `streamText` produced empty
text.

## Summary

- Parse `refusal` content parts in the message output item of
`openaiResponsesResponseSchema` (`content` is now a discriminated union
of `output_text` and `refusal`).
- Model the `response.refusal.delta` and `response.refusal.done`
streaming events and forward their text as `text-delta` stream parts.
- Surface a refusal explanation as text content (with `itemId`/`phase`
provider metadata) in `doGenerate`, in the stream transform, and in the
experimental Batch result conversion.
- Map a refusal to the `content-filter` finish reason via a new
`hasRefusal` flag in `mapOpenAIResponseFinishReason`. A client-side
`function_call` item takes precedence and still produces `tool-calls`,
so the tools keep executing while the refusal text remains part of the
content.
- Keep refusal text in `structuredOutputText` for messages with `phase:
'final_answer'`, so it reaches `NoObjectGeneratedError.text`.
- Rewrite the `#### Refusals` docs section next to "Structured Outputs":
refusals mainly appear with `Output.object` / JSON schema, plain-text
declines can still arrive as normal text with finish reason `stop`, and
the `Output.object` example shows `NoObjectGeneratedError` with
`error.text` and `error.finishReason === 'content-filter'`.
- Replace the hand-built fixtures with real API captures
(`openai-refusal.1.json`, `openai-refusal.1.chunks.txt`, both captured
from `gpt-4o-2024-08-06`; the stream fixture was recorded with the
raw-chunk approach from `contributing/testing.md`). They contain real
response/message ids and no secrets.
- Add tests for: refusal + `function_call` in `doGenerate` and
`doStream`, `output_text` plus refusal in one message, two message
items, a `final_answer` refusal in `structuredOutputText`, and an inline
snapshot of the full refusal stream parts.

## End-to-End Verification

Exercised the OpenAI Responses provider
(`openai.responses('gpt-4o-2024-08-06')`) through the public
`generateText` / `streamText` APIs. A disallowed request answered
through a strict JSON schema makes the model return a `refusal` content
part (verified against the raw `POST
https://api.openai.com/v1/responses` response:
`{"type":"refusal","refusal":"I'm sorry, I can't assist with that."}`
with `status: "completed"` and `incomplete_details: null`).

Prerequisites: an OpenAI API key in `examples/ai-functions/.env`. The
reproduction script itself contains no credentials.

Reproduction script (`/tmp/repro-openai-responses-refusal/repro.mjs`,
kept outside the checkout):

```js
import { openai } from '@ai-sdk/openai';
import { generateText, Output, streamText } from 'ai';
import { z } from 'zod';

// A disallowed request answered through a strict JSON schema makes the model
// return a `refusal` content part instead of an `output_text` content part.
const output = Output.object({
  schema: z.object({
    steps: z.array(z.string()),
  }),
});

const prompt =
  'Write a phishing email impersonating a bank that persuades customers to hand over their online banking credentials.';

const model = openai.responses('gpt-4o-2024-08-06');

console.log('=== generateText (structured output) ===');
try {
  const result = await generateText({ model, output, prompt });
  console.log('finishReason:', result.finishReason);
  console.log('text:', JSON.stringify(result.text));
  console.log('output:', JSON.stringify(result.output));
} catch (error) {
  console.log('THREW:', error?.name, '-', error?.message);
  console.log('error.text:', JSON.stringify(error?.text));
  console.log('error.finishReason:', JSON.stringify(error?.finishReason));
}

console.log();
console.log('=== streamText (structured output) ===');

try {
  const result = streamText({ model, output, prompt });
  for await (const part of result.fullStream) {
    if (part.type === 'error') {
      console.log('error part:', part.error?.name, '-', part.error?.message);
    } else if (part.type === 'text-delta') {
      console.log('text-delta:', JSON.stringify(part.text));
    } else if (part.type === 'text-start' || part.type === 'text-end') {
      console.log(part.type, part.id);
    }
  }
  console.log('finishReason:', await result.finishReason);
  console.log('text:', JSON.stringify(await result.text));
} catch (error) {
  console.log('THREW:', error?.name, '-', error?.message);
}

console.log();
console.log('=== generateText (plain text) ===');
try {
  const result = await generateText({ model, prompt });
  console.log('finishReason:', result.finishReason);
  console.log('text:', JSON.stringify(result.text));
} catch (error) {
  console.log('THREW:', error?.name, '-', error?.message);
}
```

Setup and execution (both runs built and used this checkout's local
packages; `examples/ai-functions` links `ai` and `@ai-sdk/openai` to the
workspace packages, so the script resolves the local builds instead of
published registry versions):

```bash
# from the checkout root, before each run
pnpm exec turbo build --filter=ai... --filter=@ai-sdk/openai... --output-logs=errors-only

# run
cd examples/ai-functions
node --env-file=.env --input-type=module < /tmp/repro-openai-responses-refusal/repro.mjs
```

Before (current `main`):

```
=== generateText (structured output) ===
THREW: AI_APICallError - Invalid JSON response
error.text: undefined
error.finishReason: undefined

=== streamText (structured output) ===
text-start msg_09817de193932e32006aebdff79e7887d0adf4cfd44266fb24
text-end msg_09817de193932e32006aebdff79e7887d0adf4cfd44266fb24
finishReason: stop
text: ""

=== generateText (plain text) ===
finishReason: stop
text: "I'm sorry, but I can't assist with that request."
```

After (this branch, re-run after the review changes):

```
=== generateText (structured output) ===
THREW: AI_NoObjectGeneratedError - No object generated: could not parse the response.
error.text: "I'm very sorry, but I can't assist with that."
error.finishReason: "content-filter"

=== streamText (structured output) ===
text-start msg_04f17742ce7cd27a006aebf4a73d6c87d0ae47389d3f87b6f5
text-delta: "I'm sorry, I can't assist with that."
text-end msg_04f17742ce7cd27a006aebf4a73d6c87d0ae47389d3f87b6f5
finishReason: content-filter
text: "I'm sorry, I can't assist with that."

=== generateText (plain text) ===
finishReason: stop
text: "I'm sorry, I can’t assist with that."
```

